		(uuid "0f16c4c1-2fb6-4b09-9643-c65483186149")
	)
	(text "-- VDDA & VREF+ --\nVDDA is an external analog power supply for ADCs, DACs\nand OPAMPs\nRequires two external decoupling caps 100nF and 1uF \n\nVREF+ is the external reference voltage for\nanalog peripherals\nAlso requires two external decoupling caps\n100nF and 1uF \n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 112.522 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0f50dfb9-c0a1-4ca7-934d-9b6f68860e1d")
	)
	(text "-- PDR_ON --\nPower on reset pin, connect to vdd\nto keep chip in reset mode\nuntil vdd stable >1,7v\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 147.066 73.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
			)
		)
		(uuid "117b091d-862e-45f8-be6c-27a73013fa1f")
	)
	(text "--Power MUX--\nUSB power = Input 1, Batt = Input 2\nWired such that when USB is plugged in, switches from Battery to USB\nResistor/Capacitor values and wiring taken from datasheet"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 522.732 198.628 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "14ca64cb-1c68-415f-bce6-6f81713a685d")
	)
	(text "-- VDD50USB --\nConnects to the 3.3v powering Vdd_MCU and Vdd33_USB to prevent floating\nVdd50_USB is a connection to an in chip regulator that would regualte\n5v to 3.3v for the chips USB PHY, and then Vdd33_USB would be a 3.3v \noutput of the regulator. However you can also apply 3.3v directly\nto the Vdd33_USB line, bypassing the on chip regulater. \n\nThis is useful becuase the chip specifices during startup (Vdd_MCU < 1v)\nthe vdd50_USB < Vdd_MCU + 0.3V, which may not happen as the Vdd50_USB\ncomes right from usb connection so minimal resistance/inductance\nit can reach 5v possibly faster than Vdd_MCU will reach 1V as Vdd_MCU\nneeds to go through the Power MUX, on board regulater and a lot of caps.\nThis is prevented by just using the Vdd_MCU to power USB PHY\nthrough Vdd33_USB"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 188.722 38.354 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
			)
		)
		(uuid "1582b4b1-5beb-4b1a-9ed2-f272a34db4d0")
	)
